course: dictionary
lesson: 3654
title: One small word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «First» is a small word with lots of jobs. In «first in line» it means before anyone else. In «the first day» it means number one in order. In «At first I was scared» it means at the start.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. «Everyone picked him first at football because they were scared not to» tells you first means before everyone else, because they chose him before anyone else could be chosen.
explain: «Nearly everyone is bad for the first weeks and finds practice boring sometimes» is about the early part of learning, not a race or a line. Try your meaning in the sentence: «the early weeks» fits, so you have it.
fact: «First» can be a word for before everything else, number one in order, or the start of something.
fact: «At first» means at the beginning, as in «At first I was scared».
fact: In a race, «first» means the winner. A «first» is something that has never been done before.
fact: Synonyms for the start are «initially», «at the outset» and «in the first instance».
fact: In casual talk, «first up» (Australia and New Zealand) means first of all, and «first come, first served» means the slow get nothing.
exercise: «At first I was scared, but then I loved the climbing frame.» What does first mean here? | Before everyone else in line | *At the start, at the beginning | The winner of the game | Number one in a race
exercise: «The Year 3s hid whenever Jake walked past, and everyone picked him first at football because they were scared not to.» Why were the children picking Jake first? | He had won a race | He was the first in the alphabet | *Before anyone else, because they were scared not to | It was the first day of the season
exercise: In maths, first, second and third are | Animals | Shapes | *Ordinal numbers, showing order (1st, 2nd, 3rd) | Colours
test: «Nearly everyone is bad for the first weeks and finds practice boring sometimes.» What does first mean here? | Weeks with a race | *The early weeks, at the start | The last weeks | Holiday weeks
test: Which of these is a first? | A school that wins a trophy every year | *Our school's first robot race, something never done before | A word we all know well | Something we do every single day for years
exam: In the exam voice, which word means «at the start»? | Primarily | Finally | Lastly | *Initially
